<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher icon's foreground: the Fool pathway's sigil.

  Two hand-drawn versions came before this and both looked like clipart. The
  first stacked an eye on a rounded-square die - too many marks for 48dp, and
  the die's corner arcs rendered malformed on device. The second dropped the
  die and kept the eye, which was cleaner and still generic: thin strokes, three
  nested circles and six rays, all of which turn to mush at launcher size.

  The lesson is about ICONS rather than about this icon. A launcher mark is
  read at 48dp, so it survives on silhouette and contrast, not on detail; and
  original geometry is only worth drawing when there is nothing better to point
  at. Here there is. The Fool is the setting's first pathway and its emblem is
  already in this app, drawn by people who draw for a living.

  The licence is the one recorded in PathwayArt - the publisher's artwork, kept
  under an exception the repository's owner took deliberately. This puts it on
  the home screen, which is a more prominent use than the pathway chooser, and
  is noted here so that decision stays visible rather than drifting.

  Inset 12dp a side rather than the 18dp that would put the DRAWABLE exactly on
  the 72dp safe zone. The sigil carries its own transparent margin, so its
  visible mark sits well inside its bounds; measuring the safe zone against the
  file rather than against the ink left the crown small in the tile.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/pathway_fool"
    android:insetLeft="12dp"
    android:insetTop="12dp"
    android:insetRight="12dp"
    android:insetBottom="12dp" />
